    "intro_html":  "Kadai chicken is named after the pan it is cooked in, a deep steel wok that gets ripping hot. The technique is bhuna: cook the tomato and spices down hard until the oil separates and the masala clings to the meat instead of swimming around it. No cream sauce to hide behind, no coconut milk. The spice blend is coarsely crushed, not powdered, so you get little bursts of coriander and chile as you eat. Each bowl comes in at \u003cstrong\u003e566 calories and 32 grams of protein\u003c/strong\u003e for about \u003cstrong\u003e$3.55\u003c/strong\u003e (at everyday cost).",
